    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n82444" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιφαν-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>seen all round</i>, of a
			city, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.102
			</span></i> ; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ζῷα</span> figures
				<i>standing free and unattached</i>, opp. those in relief,
				<i><span class="en">
				Callix.
				2
			</span></i>, cf.<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>conspicuous, notorious</i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>Aj.</u>
				66
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. τὰ πράγματα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Lys.</u>
					756
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">π. ἀδίκημα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lys.
					9.22
				</span></i>
